# Written once by studyforge's execution skill, with defaults; from then on this
# file is yours, and no regeneration writes over it. Set the ports here by hand,
# or with the skill's record step, which checks every value first.
# This instance's compose project, host ports and container names: the one
# place a port is set. Each is checked before anything is served: a port
# outside 1-65535, one port for two services, or a name that is not one word
# is refused by `studyforge serve` and by the compose preflight, by its name.
STUDYFORGE_PROJECT=studyforge-claude-senior-java-engineer-interview-preparation
STUDYFORGE_EDITOR_PORT=8444
STUDYFORGE_EDITOR_NAME=studyforge-claude-senior-java-engineer-interview-preparation-editor-1
STUDYFORGE_RUNNER_NAME=studyforge-runner-claude-senior-java-engineer-interview-preparation
STUDYFORGE_SITE_PORT=8772
STUDYFORGE_SITE_NAME=studyforge-site-claude-senior-java-engineer-interview-preparation
